///1CRC

CRC.CMD - CP/M-86 Version 6.4
by Bill Bolton     (10/30/84)

This program will compute the CRC values of a specified file or
group of files.  It can display the values to the CRT, check the
values against a file called CRCKLIST.CRC, create the disk file
called CRCKLIST.CRC, or all of these.


///2USAGE
To calculate the CRC of a given file use the form:          CRC filename.typ

To calculate the CRC of a group of files use:               CRC *.typ

To calculate the CRC of ALL files on a disk or area use:    CRC *.*


///2CREATE
To create a disk file called CRCKLIST.CRC use:              CRC *.* F


///2COMPARE
To compare the values against the file CRCKLIST.CRC use:    CRC <CR>

...and ALL files will be checked against the original CRC values put
into the file CRCKLIST.CRC.  If they match, a message "**match**"
will be displayed for each file.  The total matches will also be
displayed at the end of the process, as well as "no-matches".
